; An include lists each directory once per parse and serves later includes
; from that listing.  Which files match must not depend on that: a literal
; include repeated, a glob over the same directory, a literal after the
; glob, and a glob in a middle component all see the same files as before.
; a.dat is read three times (twice by name, once by the glob), b.dat twice
; (glob and name), c.dat twice (glob in the middle component and name).

include include-listing-cache/a.dat
include include-listing-cache/a.dat
include include-listing-cache/*.dat
include include-listing-cache/b.dat
include include-listing-cache/s*/c.dat
include include-listing-cache/sub/c.dat

test bal
             $-15.00  Assets:Cash
              $15.00  Expenses
               $3.00    A
               $4.00    B
               $8.00    C
--------------------
                   0
end test
